        "type": "grade",
        "dimensionId": "fiscal-health",
        "dimensionName": "Fiscal Health",
        "from": "D",
        "to": "C",
        "deltaLabel": "+1 letter",
        "headline": "Fiscal Health moved D → C",
        "body": "The Spring Economic Update lowered the projected FY 2025-26 deficit to $66.9B, and PBO now says both fiscal anchors are on track. The file stops at C because the deficit remains above the B threshold and PBO still flags capital-budgeting, interest-burden, and defence-cost caveats.",
        "drivers": [
          "PBO says the deficit-to-GDP anchor is on track, declining from 2.1% in 2025-26 to 1.4% by 2030-31",
          "PBO says the operating-balance anchor is projected to be met by 2028-29",
          "Caveats remain on capital-budgeting definitions, rising interest burden, and omitted anticipated defence spending"
        ],
        "link": {
          "label": "PBO fiscal anchors assessment",
          "href": "https://www.pbo-dpb.ca/en/publications/NT-2627-002-S--pbo-assessment-spring-economic-update-fiscal-anchors-fiscal-sustainability--evaluation-dpb-mise-jour-economique-printemps-cibles-budgetaires-viabilite-financiere"
